# Images (always WebP)

Content images on the site are **WebP only**. Do not copy PNG, JPEG, or GIF into `public/projects`, `public/writing`, or other content folders. Convert with the scripts, then point MDX at the `.webp` path.

Platform icons stay as they are: `app/icon.png`, `app/favicon.ico`, `app/apple-icon.png`, `public/icon-192.png`, `public/icon-512.png`. Flat vector logos may stay SVG. `docs/` is not site content.

Do not use chat attachments as a source to enlarge — Cursor often saves them at 1024px. If a cover is smaller than 1920×1080, stop and ask for a larger export.

## Covers (project and article)

Same spec. Recenter-crop, never upscale.

| Use | Path | Size |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Project cover | `public/projects/<slug>/cover.webp` | **1920×1080** |
| Article cover | `public/writing/<slug>/cover.webp` | **1920×1080** |

```bash
pnpm optimize-cover -- <input> public/projects/<slug>/cover.webp
pnpm optimize-cover -- <input> public/writing/<slug>/cover.webp
```

Frontmatter: `image: '/projects/<slug>/cover.webp'` or `image: '/writing/<slug>/cover.webp'`. Do not repeat the cover as the first `![]()` in the MDX body. The page renders it.

## In-article images

Also WebP. Do not force 16:9.

| Use | Path | Max width |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Photo in the text column | `public/writing/<slug>/` | **1600px** |
| UI screenshot or `#wide` breakout | `public/writing/<slug>/` or `public/projects/<slug>/` | **1920px** |

```bash
pnpm optimize-image -- <input> public/writing/<slug>/name.webp --max 1600
pnpm optimize-image -- <input> public/writing/<slug>/name.webp --max 1920
```

```mdx
![Alt text](/writing/my-slug/name.webp "Caption")
![Alt text](/writing/my-slug/name.webp#wide "Caption")
```

## Rendering

- Covers and article images go through `next/image` with real `width`/`height` from `getPublicImageSize`
- Do not use a raw `<img>` for post content
- Keep `next.config.mjs` `images.formats` as AVIF then WebP
